WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Two people can see the same crash and answer differently because of one word in the question.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
In 1974, psychologists studied that difference, then asked about broken glass that was not in the film.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
A vivid report isn't always a recording. It can also contain later interpretation.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Try twelve minutes of quiet observation. Mark what you noticed and what you inferred.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Want audio structure instead of silence? Zen12 sells twelve-minute tracks in several listening styles.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
The recordings are not proven to repair memory. Compare formats and evidence before you choose.
